    "result": "`add_business_days` is implemented in `solution.py`, and the 5 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I didn't run a coverage report. The tests exercise every branch of the function, so coverage should be well above 90%.\n\nIt follows `spec.md`:\n- **Direction:** `n > 0` and `n < 0` step forward or backward, never counting `start`. `n == 0` returns `start` if it's a business day, otherwise the next one.\n- **Validation:** `start` must be a `date`, not a `datetime`. `n` must be an `int`, so `bool` and `float` are rejected. Each holiday must also be a plain `date`. All of these raise `TypeError`.\n- **Holidays:** any iterable works, including a generator. A holiday that falls on a weekend changes nothing.\n\nThe tests cover forward, backward and zero cases, weekend starts, holiday skipping with a list, a generator and a set, and the `TypeError` cases.",
